#1 Escapes

Backslash + syntax = literal. Backslash + other = stays.

#1.1 Inline style

\**not bold\**, \__not italic\__, \==not underline\==, \~~not strike\~~.

\`not code\`, \[not link\], \![not image\], \|not pipe.

\/'not comment'\/.

#1.2 Links and images

Escaped `\|` and `\]` stay inside.

[https://example.com|a\|b]
[https://example.com|label with \] bracket]

![https://example.com/a.jpg|alt\]text]

#1.3 Block prefixes

Backslash stops blocks.

\> not quote
\> still paragraph

\#1 not heading

\* not list
\+ not list
\- not list
\^ not list
\= not list

\--- not rule

\<! not codeblock

\1. not ordered list

\| not gutter

#1.4 Backslash itself

\\ = one backslash.

C:\path stays. \a stays. Trailing \

#1.5 Verbatim zones

No unescape in code.

`code \* stays`

/' hidden '/

/' a \'/ b '/ after comment
